  "provenance": "Repo-local descriptor (the converter's own repo, litert-community/MiniCPM-V-4.7-1B). Backends and context come from the repo's litertlm_manifest.json. The three files share the decoder bytes (a Qwen3.5-style hybrid: a new conversation on a loaded model continues from the previous one's state, LiteRT-LM #3165, so an app opens one conversation per load). vl_int8 has the fp16 vision encoder: gpu runs the decoder and the vision encoder on the GPU (the card's Galaxy S26 row with the vision encoder on the GPU), gpu_vision_cpu keeps the vision encoder on the CPU, cpu runs both on the CPU. vl_int8vis has the int8 vision encoder and declares cpu only: it was made for the 8 GB Pixel 8a, where the card measured it on the CPU and the decoder's GPU engine did not build within the card's 400,000 kB memory line; its GPU path has not been measured on a phone. int8 is the text-only file; the manifest names cpu as its default backend and lists it as not run on a phone.",
